  "notes": "Every 8x8 ground tile of the overworld. Solid: water, reeds, trunks, the deep forest, boulders, big rocks, fences, ledges, ruin walls, pillars and graves. Grass, tall grass, flowers, paths, stairs and stone floors are walkable. Paths and water have edge and corner pieces. Tiles: 'a' grass, 'b' grass with tufts, 'c' grass with a few tufts, 'd' tall grass, 'e' tall grass (offset), 'f' red flowers, 'g' white flowers, 'h' yellow flowers, 'i' path C, 'j' path N, 'k' path S, 'l' path E, 'm' path W, 'n' path NE, 'o' path NW, 'p' path SE, 'q' path SW, 'r' path iNE, 's' path iNW, 't' path iSE, 'u' path iSW, 'v' water C, 'w' water N, 'x' water S, 'y' water E, 'z' water W, 'A' water NE, 'B' water NW, 'C' water SE, 'D' water SW, 'E' water iNE, 'F' water iNW, 'G' water iSE, 'H' water iSW, 'I' tree trunk (left), 'J' tree trunk (right), 'K' deep forest floor, 'L' boulder, 'M' rock tl, 'N' rock tr, 'O' rock bl, 'P' rock br, 'Q' fence, 'R' ledge top, 'S' ledge wall, 'T' ledge foot, 'U' stone stairs, 'V' ruin wall top, 'W' ruin wall, 'X' pillar top, 'Y' pillar base, 'Z' grave, '0' stone floor, '1' cracked stone floor, '2' mossy stone floor, '3' circle 0, '4' circle 1, '5' circle 2, '6' circle 3.",
